WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.903
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.404
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:08.375
Well, guys, today is July 27th,
and you know what that means.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.442 line:0%
-99 days.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.710 line:0%
-99 days.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.978 line:0%
-99 days.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.815 line:0%
-99 days away from
the presidential election.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:19.953
-That's right -- we are just
99 days away from election

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.555
and just 100 days away
from President Trump

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.358
declaring the results invalid.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.927
Yep, just 99 days
or, as one man put it,

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:31.463
[ Russian accent ] "So much
hacking, so little time."

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:34.100
[ Normal voice ] Trump thinks
99 days is plenty of time

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.035
to get his campaign in shape.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.171
He's like someone looking in
the mirror in June going,

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.640
"I've still got time
for swimsuit season."

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.042
99 days.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:48.982
That's like an entire baseball
season plus 96 days.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:52.418
Yeah, 99 days
doesn't seem like that much.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:56.555
Then again, the last 99 days
have felt like 900 years, so...

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:59.392
The clock is ticking on Trump's
chances to turn things around.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.927
Today, he saw his approval
rating in the low 30s

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:05.632
and spent the morning screaming
into his MyPillow.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.100
With just 99 days left,
it looks like Joe Biden

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.703
is choose --
close to choosing -- Sorry.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.438
I got screwed because no one
laughed at that last one,

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.939
but it's alright.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.409
I know, but if you hear it --
Maybe if you hear it at home --

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.878
-What's MyPillow?
-It was so funny!

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.346
-The MyPillow
guy is the guy that --

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.882
It's his, like, biggest
supporter, yeah, is MyPillow.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:26.352
[ Laugh track ]
No, it's too late.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.388
-Keep it in there.
-No, no.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.790
-Oh, it's good.
-It's not worth it.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.459
Well, with just 99 days left,
it looks like Joe Biden

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:36.095
is close to choosing
a running mate this week,

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.864
and he's now personally
interviewing all the candidates.

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:40.934
He said, "I'm going to ask you
the same question

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:45.638
Obama asked me -- do you know
how to play the quiet game?"

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.073
That's right -- Joe is asking
the hard-hitting questions like,

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:50.276
"Do you have organize experience
organizing pills?"

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.644
Stuff like that.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.846
It will be a wake-up call
when Biden says,

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.447
"Where do you see yourself
in five years?",

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:59.385
and the candidates are like,
"President."

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.220
Well, guys, over the weekend,
while discussing

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.888
Trump's response to
the pandemic,

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:05.691
Nancy Pelosi said that her new
nickname for Trump is

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:08.761
"Mr. Make Matters Worse."

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.231
For more, I'm joined by
Kevin Cipriano,

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.199
the person who writes
the clever nicknames

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.833
that Nancy Pelosi uses.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:20.239 line:0%
Hey. Kevin, How did you come up
with the nickname

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:22.742 line:0%
Mr. Make Matters Worse?

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.845 line:0%
-Well, first, I started with
Trump's gender, which is man.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.780 line:0%
So that's where I got
the "Mr." part.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.782 line:0%
And as far as the
"Makes Matters Worse" part,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.984 line:0%
I thought, "What is Trump
doing that's upsetting

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.819 line:0%
so many people right now?"

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:35.054
And that's obvious.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.090
It's the way
he handles matters, right?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.893
And what does he do to matters?
Well, he makes them worse.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.229
And that's how the
famous nickname was born.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:47.767
Now everyone calls Trump
"Mr. Make Matters Worse."

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:52.271
-I don't think anyone but Pelosi
is calling him that.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.907
No offense,
but people are saying

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.008
it's not the best nickname ever.

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:57.977
-Well, it's not my
proudest work.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.145
I came up with a nickname
for Betsy DeVos

00:03:00.145 --> 00:03:01.814
that's pretty devastating.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.884
You know how she's
the Secretary of Education?

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.252
-Yeah.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.354
-Well, my nickname for her --

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:14.460
"The Secretary of Miseducation
of the American People."

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.797 line:0%
-Yeah, I think you're hitting
the same wall there.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.032 line:0%
Nicknames are usually catchy.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.868
-Well, I only have to answer to
Speaker Pelosi,

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.438
and let me tell you,
these names are very funny

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:28.641
to an 80-year-old woman
who is extremely stressed.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.643
-That's great,
but just as an example,

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.878
Dwayne Johnson's nickname
was "The Rock,"

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:34.146
not "The Large Man Who is

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:36.182
Good at Both Punching
and Acting."

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:40.586
-Okay. Fine, Jimmy.
I'll come clean.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.554
I know these names aren't good.
I get it.

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:44.390
But Nancy loves them.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.092
She told me the key to
a great nickname

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.027
is for it to be --
and I quote --

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.997
"Very long and also
impossible to remember."

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:54.033
Being Nancy Pelosi's
nickname writer is my dream job.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.734
Don't ruin this for me.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:58.971
-Hey, it's okay. I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to upset you.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.507
-Maybe I can run
some other nicknames by you,

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.744
and you tell me if you think
Speaker Pelosi would like them.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.946 line:0%
-Yeah. Sure.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.448 line:0%
I mean, it seems she and I
have different tastes,

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.617 line:0%
but, yeah, let's give it a shot.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:13.019
-Okay, this one's for
Steve Scalise,

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.353
who's a member of the House.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.387
[ Clears throat ]

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:16.989
Member of the house, huh?

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:18.991
More like "Member of the House,

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:24.096
and The House is a House
of Cards that is Tumbling Down."

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:27.133 line:0%
-That's all one nickname?

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.568
-Loud and clear, Jimmy.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.736
But this next one is
a perfect burn.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.371
It's for Mike Pence.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.340
"The Vice Presi-don't

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:40.580
of the Un-United States
of Ameri-don't."

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.615 line:0%
-Not sure I completely
get that one.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.249 line:0%
I think you have better stuff.

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:45.785
-Okay, Mitch McConnell --

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:51.290
"Captain of the S.S. Nonsense,
All Aboard, Toot-toot!"

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.627 line:0%
-You pronounce "comma" in the --
Look, it seems like

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.596 line:0%
the other ones
Pelosi likes, kind of,

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:59.498 line:0%
so I won't say it's good,
but maybe she'll like that one.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.667
-Jimmy, you just saved
my career.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.536
Now I can go back to
helping the Democrats

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.238
fight the Trump administration
the best way we know how --

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.674
with sass.

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:11.611 line:0%
[ Imitates sizzling, laughs ]
-Kevin Cipriano, everybody.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:15.181 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:18.517
And get this --
the other day, Trump said

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:20.086
that he'd be throwing out
the first pitch

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.520
at a Yankees game next month.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.556
Let's see how those plans
are holding up.

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.092 line:0%
-President Trump says
he won't be throwing out

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.559 line:0%
the first pitch at
Yankee Stadium

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.362 line:0%
on August 15th after all.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.331 line:0%
The president tweeted that
he's focusing on

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.066 line:0%
coronavirus meetings
and the economy

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.466 line:0%
and can't be there that day.

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:37.202
-Yeah. Trump won't be throwing
out the first pitch.

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:39.205
Although, thanks to
his handling of the pandemic,

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.306
he might be able to throw out

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:45.211
the last pitch
of the season tomorrow.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:50.115
I wish Trump didn't cancel,
mostly because I wanted to see

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:52.852
him slowly walk down
the pitcher's mound.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:57.356
[ As Trump ] See, the dirt
is very slippery --

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:01.494
very, very slippery --
and I'm wearing leather shoes.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:04.997
And everyone knows,
when you wear leather shoes

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:08.468
on slippery pitcher's mounds,

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:12.571
it's hard to get down
off the mound.

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:14.006
[ Normal voice ]
It's kind of sad that Trump

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.307
cancelled throwing the ball.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:16.742
When he heard that,
Don Jr. was like,

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.711
"Eh, you get used to it."

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.752
Well, Trump
skipping the first pitch

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:29.155
isn't the news baseball fans
are upset about today.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.756
The season's
just a few days old,

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.558
